4669   1B40             
4670   1B40             ; Character block shapes table using setB.
4671   1B40             ; Parts of the mothership's purple conveyor belt.
4672   1B40             ; So an ordinary belt hit:
4673   1B40             ; 1. Consumes the bullet (`AND $F7`).
4674   1B40             ; 2. Sets the "mother-ship hit" flag `$4366` -> plays the hit sound; no score is awarded.
4675   1B40             ; 3. Swaps the hit tile for a "damaged" belt tile from `T1B40/T1B48/T1B50`,
4676   1B40             ;    chosen by the bullet's X position (left/right half) and the tile's low nibble
4677   1B40             ;     — so the belt visibly chips/breaks apart where you shoot it.
4678   1B40             T1B40:
4679   1B40 6C                                 .DB $6C
4680   1B41 6D                                 .DB $6D
4681   1B42 6E                                 .DB $6E
4682   1B43 6F                                 .DB $6F
4683   1B44             
4684   1B48                                    .ORG $1B48
