8915   3BB0             
8916   3BB0             ; Wing mask table:
8917   3BB0             ; The wing table base is `$3BB0` and it's indexed by `B`, but the wing test only runs for `B >= $20`.
8918   3BB0             ; So the addresses actually consulted are:
8919   3BB0             ;  - `B = $20` -> `$3BB0 + $20` = `$3BD0` (bird character `$B0`)
8920   3BB0             ;  - `B = $4F` -> `$3BB0 + $4F` = `$3BFF` (bird character `$DF`)
8921   3BB0             ; Entries `$3BB0`–`$3BCF` (which would correspond to `B < $20`) are never reached,
8922   3BB0             ; they're the dead lower part of the wing table. `$3BD0`–`$3BFF` are the real,
8923   3BB0             ; in use wing masks, one per bird shape in the `$B0`–`$DF` character range.
8924   3BB0             T3BB0:
8925   3BB0 03 E0 03 E0                        .DB $03, $E0, $03, $E0, $0F, $80, $0F, $00, $3C, $00, $1E, $3F, $00, $FC, $F0, $00   ; for bird background tiles E0 - EF
8925   3BB4 0F 80 0F 00 
8925   3BB8 3C 00 1E 3F 
8925   3BBC 00 FC F0 00 
8926   3BC0 7F FE 00 F0                        .DB $7F, $FE, $00, $F0, $03, $E0, $00, $00, $0F, $80, $00, $00, $3F, $00, $FE, $30   ; for bird background tiles F0 - FF
8926   3BC4 03 E0 00 00 
8926   3BC8 0F 80 00 00 
8926   3BCC 3F 00 FE 30 
8927   3BD0             
