8985   3DC0             ; Scroll-phase -> active-object-window table for the bird wave.
8986   3DC0             ; Used by `L3930`, which runs every frame during the bird attack waves (it's called from the wave loop at `$3431` and `$3448`).
8987   3DC0             ; It defines a sliding, resizing window over the column of bird objects as a function of how far the wave has scrolled down.
8988   3DC0             ; - Phases 0–8: the window starts at the top object (`$4B70`) and grows `6 -> 7 -> 8` as more rows enter the play field.
8989   3DC0             ; - Phases 10–22: the start pointer slides down one object at a time (`$4B78 -> $4B80 -> ... -> $4BA8`),
8990   3DC0             ;                 while the count shrinks `7 -> 6 -> ... -> 1`, modeling the top rows scrolling out / fewer rows remaining active.
8991   3DC0             ; - Phases 24–30: it wraps back to the top (`$4B70`) and grows again `2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5`.
8992   3DC0             T3DC0:
8993   3DC0 06 70                              .DB $06, M4B70 & $FF         ; phase  0 : count=6, ptr=$4B70
8994   3DC2 07 70                              .DB $07, M4B70 & $FF         ; phase  2 : count=7, ptr=$4B70
8995   3DC4 08 70                              .DB $08, M4B70 & $FF         ; phase  4 : count=8, ptr=$4B70
8996   3DC6 08 70                              .DB $08, M4B70 & $FF         ; phase  6 : count=8, ptr=$4B70
